KeywordAbility(
    name: "protection",
    params: [Quality],
    spelling: "protection",
    grammar: FixedKeyword(
        surface: "protection",
        parameter: Quality(preposition: ("Preposition", "From")),
    ),
    // STOP. "Protection from [quality]" [CR#702.16a] is four consequences, and three
    // of them write cleanly: can't be targeted by spells with the quality or by
    // abilities from a source with it [CR#702.16b] as a `DeonticRule` over
    // `Core(Target)` in the patient role; damage from such sources prevented
    // [CR#702.16e] as a `DamageRule`; and an attacking creature can't be blocked by
    // such creatures [CR#702.16f] as a `DeonticRule` over `Core(Block)`. Written out
    // with all three, `Abbey Gargoyles` proved. The fourth cannot be written: "can't
    // be enchanted by Auras that have the stated quality" and "can't be equipped by
    // Equipment … or fortified by Fortifications that have the stated quality"
    // [CR#702.16c,702.16d] is a prohibition over the `Attach` deed, whose registry row
    // gives it an agent role of `playerAgent` and NO patient role at all, so
    // `deedFits` refuses every noun phrase in that slot — `Abbey Gargoyles` refused
    // with `[Semantics.Refusal.deedFits, Semantics.Refusal.deonticPatientOk]` and
    // proved as soon as that row came out. This is the shape Indestructible's
    // `Destroy` patient role already carries: fixing it is a change to a deed's role
    // columns, which this ticket's overlay authority does not cover. A body carrying
    // only three of the four rows would be a wrong analysis, so none is written.
    body: Keyword(keyword: "Protection", params: [Quality(Param(0))], body: []),
)
